    a: "A systematic, ongoing process for capturing, tagging, and synthesizing customer feedback across many channels (support tickets, sales calls, NPS comments, community forums, interviews) into structured themes the product team can act on — as opposed to ad hoc collection where feedback arrives inconsistently and gets lost in inboxes or forgotten Slack threads. A mature VoC program includes a consistent taxonomy for tagging feedback by theme/segment/severity, a regular synthesis cadence, and a visible loop back to whoever raised the feedback about what happened with it.",
