    q: "What's the difference between activation and retention, and why do PMs distinguish them?",
    a: "Activation is whether a new user reaches the point of experiencing the product's core value for the first time (often a specific, measurable event — 'uploaded first file,' 'sent first message') — it's a one-time, early-lifecycle milestone. Retention is whether users keep coming back and using the product over an extended period after that. They're distinguished because they have different root causes and fixes: a low activation rate points to onboarding/first-run experience problems, while low retention despite good activation points to ongoing value/habit-formation problems — conflating them leads to fixing the wrong stage of the funnel.",
