    lvl: "easy",
    q: "A stakeholder asks you to add a specific competitor's exact feature list to your product vision document. Explain in 2 sentences why you'd push back.",
    sol: "'A vision document describes the customer problem and future state we're aiming for, not a feature checklist — pulling in a competitor's specific feature list would tie our vision to matching them rather than to solving our target customer's actual problem, which might need a different solution entirely. I'll capture the competitive gap separately in our competitive analysis, and we can decide feature-by-feature whether it's actually relevant to our strategy.'",
    exp: "Keeps the vision document at the right level of abstraction (problem/future-state) rather than letting it collapse into a reactive feature-parity list.",
