    q: "A stakeholder shows you a persona slide with only demographics (age, income, location, job title) and asks for your feedback before it's used to guide a roadmap decision. What's missing, and what 2 questions would you ask to fix it?",
    sol: "Missing: the actual job/goal this person is trying to accomplish, their current workarounds/frustrations, and what would make them switch or adopt — demographics alone rarely predict product decisions. Questions: 1) 'What specific task or goal does this person struggle with today that we're trying to help with?' 2) 'What research (interviews, usage data, support tickets) is this persona actually based on, versus assumption?'",
