    q: "Sketch a 5-stage customer journey map for a user signing up for and using a project-management SaaS tool for the first month, and name the single stage most likely to have the highest drop-off risk for a typical B2B SaaS product.",
    sol: "Stages: 1) Awareness (finds the product via search/referral) 2) Signup (creates account) 3) Onboarding (first setup — inviting teammates, creating first project) 4) First value moment (completes a first meaningful workflow, e.g. assigns and completes a task) 5) Habitual use (returns regularly without prompting). Highest drop-off risk: Onboarding — this is typically where the gap between 'signed up out of curiosity' and 'actually integrated into daily workflow' is widest, and where friction (empty states, unclear setup steps, no teammates invited yet) most commonly causes silent abandonment before the product ever gets a fair chance to prove value.",
