    sol: "Empathize: interview/observe commuters who've missed stops — what were they doing, why didn't they notice. Define: 'Commuters engrossed in audio content lose track of their location and miss their intended stop, especially on unfamiliar or repetitive routes.' Ideate: brainstorm wide — a haptic alert, an auto-pause-and-announce feature, a visual countdown widget, a location-based volume-lowering nudge — without judging feasibility yet. Prototype: build a low-fidelity mockup of the top 1-2 ideas (e.g. a paper/clickable mockup of a haptic-alert setting screen). Test: have real commuters try the prototype on an actual commute or a realistic simulation, and observe whether they actually notice and act on the alert in time.",
