    q: "You want to redesign a settings page's navigation. Design a simple open card-sorting exercise (in 3 steps) to inform the new structure.",
    sol: "1) Write each individual setting/feature currently in the settings area on its own card (physical or digital, e.g. via a tool like Optimal Workshop). 2) Ask 8-10 representative users, individually, to group the cards into categories that make sense to THEM and label each group in their own words — with no predefined categories given. 3) Analyze patterns across participants (which items consistently get grouped together, what labels recur) to inform the new navigation structure, rather than designing it around how the internal team currently mentally organizes the settings.",
