    q: "Give one example of a 'delighter' (Kano model) feature and explain why it wouldn't work as a 'must-be' feature for the same product.",
    sol: "Example: a food-delivery app that occasionally includes a surprise personalized note or a small unexpected discount with no announcement. It wouldn't work as a 'must-be' because if it were expected/always-on, users would stop noticing it as delightful and would instead treat its absence as a defect — delighters specifically rely on being unexpected to produce disproportionate satisfaction.",
