    q: "Compute a RICE score for a feature with: Reach = 2000 users/quarter, Impact = 2 (high), Confidence = 80%, Effort = 4 person-months. Show the calculation.",
    sol: "RICE = (Reach x Impact x Confidence) / Effort = (2000 x 2 x 0.8) / 4 = 3200 / 4 = 800. Score = 800.",
    exp: "The formula rewards high reach/impact estimated with real confidence, penalized by effort — a score is only meaningful relative to other initiatives scored the same way, not in isolation.",
