    lvl: "easy",
    q: "A PM is asked to estimate a story in story points during planning poker, but they're not on the engineering team. What should they do?",
    sol: "Decline to estimate the technical effort themselves — story points reflect the team's own relative sizing judgment based on complexity/uncertainty they understand better than the PM does. The PM's role in that moment is answering clarifying questions about scope/requirements that affect the estimate (not picking a number), and, once the team's estimate is in, using it to inform sequencing/prioritization decisions.",
    exp: "A PM inserting their own point estimate (or worse, pressuring the team toward a number that fits a deadline) undermines the whole point of the team estimating its own work based on what they know about the implementation.",
