    sol: "Since revenue = (new revenue from new customers) + (expansion) - (contraction) - (churn), and new-customer-driven revenue is up, the offsetting decline must be in expansion, contraction, or churn — check each: has churned MRR increased (segment by cohort/plan/tenure to find where), has expansion MRR from existing customers slowed or reversed (fewer upgrades, more downgrades — check by plan tier and by how long customers have been on the platform), or has average new-customer contract value itself dropped even as customer COUNT rose (e.g. winning smaller deals, more discounting) masking the acquisition win. Once the specific offsetting branch is identified (e.g. 'churn among month-13+ cohorts has doubled'), propose a targeted investigation into that specific segment's root cause rather than a broad, undirected retention initiative.",
